course: dictionary
lesson: 1469
title: Catalogue: a list of things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A catalogue is a list of things, usually in order and often with pictures or details. «You can find any book in the library catalogue.» The word list is the clue: a catalogue helps you look things up quickly.
explain: The word can also mean a booklet or website of things to buy. «Mum let me look through the toy catalogue and order a kite.» Look through and order are clues that the catalogue shows goods you can buy.
explain: As a verb, to catalogue means to make a careful, ordered list. «More than a million asteroids have been catalogued.» Astronomers listed them carefully so they can be studied. Swap in listed to check: the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A catalogue is a list of things, often with pictures and details.
fact: A library catalogue lists the library's books and shows which shelf each one is on.
fact: A catalogue can also be a booklet or website showing things you can buy, such as toys or clothes.
fact: «Catalogued» means listed in a careful, ordered way.
fact: US spelling is catalog, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: What is a library catalogue? | A quiet room for reading | *A list of the library's books, showing where each one is | A book about cats | A shelf in the corner
exercise: «More than a million asteroids have been catalogued.» Which word means listed carefully? | *catalogued | million | asteroids | have
exercise: Mum says, «Let's order a kite from the catalogue.» What is the catalogue? | A school bell | *A booklet or website showing things you can buy | A pile of old newspapers | A map of the stars
test: «Many bright stars have Arabic names, because astronomers kept Greek star catalogues.» What does catalogues mean here? | Shooting stars | Cloudy nights | Telescopes | *Ordered lists of stars
test: For a project, which one shows which shelf a book is on? | A bookmark | The index | *The library catalogue | The contents page
exam: «A real book can be found in a library catalogue.» Why is the catalogue useful for checking a book is real? | *It is a list where real books can be found | It is made of paper | It tells you the weather | It has a cover picture
